SWEET AOC pre-load probe (patch 0161, plan 2026-11-14 oneshot-2 step A4), boot-arg sweetaoc=1. READS ONLY: aoc_req 0x175D0000
(+0x00, +0x40), the GSA mailbox 0x17C90000 mask/status/shared registers, the ACPM channel 13 descriptor and queue pointers in APM SRAM
0x02039000, the AOC SysMMU 0x1A090000 CTRL/CFG/STATUS/VERSION/CAPA. Every block is one the stock kernel claims (ref iomem.txt); the AOC
S2MPU 0x1A0B0000 is not read (no stock claim, XNU has no fault-safe read). Cites in bsd/dev/sweet_aoc.h (host test shim/aoc_pre_host_test.c).
Hooked at the top of sweet_trusty_init (patch 0156), before any secure-world call. Lines "SWEET AOC PRE: ...", last
"SWEET AOC PRE: verdict PASS|FAIL reads=N". Without the boot-arg nothing changes.

